---
// NOTE: Generated template. Review and validate legally before production.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const locale = 'en';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const lastUpdated = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' }).format(new Date());
const toc = [
  { id: 'what', label: 'What are cookies?' },
  { id: 'uses', label: 'Does Baldurion use cookies?' },
  { id: 'analytics', label: 'Analytics cookies' },
  { id: 'localstorage', label: 'What Baldurion stores in your browser' },
  { id: 'embeds', label: 'Third-party embeds' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Baldurion only sets analytics cookies, and only if you accept them. Find out what we store in your browser and why."
  locale={locale}
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="what">What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small files that some websites store in your browser to remember information (preferences, sessions, tracking). There are different types depending on their purpose and duration.</p>

  <h2 id="uses">Does Baldurion use cookies?</h2>
  <p><strong>Only analytics cookies, and only if you accept them.</strong> We set no advertising, remarketing or profiling cookies, first-party or third-party.</p>
  <p>Google Analytics is loaded on every page with consent <em>denied</em> by default, so it writes nothing to your browser. It starts setting cookies only after you press <em>Accept</em> in the privacy banner. If you reject, or simply never choose, no analytics cookie is ever created. If you accept and later change your mind, we delete the ones already set.</p>

  <h2 id="analytics">Analytics cookies</h2>
  <p>These exist only after you have given consent:</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Provider</th><th>Duration</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google Analytics 4</td><td>2 years</td><td>Tell one visitor apart from another</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>_ga_B543SXCHWQ</code></td><td>Google Analytics 4</td><td>2 years</td><td>Keep the state of your session</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>You can withdraw your consent whenever you like from the <a href={`${base}preferences/`}>preferences page</a>: analytics stops immediately and these cookies are deleted.</p>

  <h2 id="localstorage">What Baldurion stores in your browser</h2>
  <p>We use <code>localStorage</code>, which is <strong>not a cookie</strong>. It is a modern browser API that allows storing preferences without sending them to any server.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Key</th><th>Content</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>baldurion_theme</code></td><td>"light" or "dark"</td><td>Remember your preferred theme</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>baldurion_locale</code></td><td>"es", "en" or "pl"</td><td>Remember your language</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>baldurion_loaded_embeds</code></td><td>JSON with IDs</td><td>Not ask you to activate embeds again</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>baldurion_consent_analytics</code></td><td>"granted" or "denied"</td><td>Remember your analytics decision so we do not ask again</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>This data only exists in your browser, is not sent to Baldurion or third parties, and you can delete it at any time from your browser settings or from the <a href={`${base}preferences/`}>preferences page</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="embeds">Third-party embeds</h2>
  <p>YouTube, Spotify, Twitter and Instagram embeds <strong>can set cookies</strong> when you activate them. That is why they do not load automatically. They only activate if you consciously click on each one.</p>
  <p>For more information on data handling, see our <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
